  "status_text": "One flip of a signal from yes to no can now save more and more gates as a graph grows, and both halves of that are checked. For every n from 2, the n by n graph joining u to v when exactly one of u = i and v = j is the case needs exactly 2n - 1 AND/OR gates of fan-in two on one-a-side inputs [L-meta-19121], yet has a circuit of at most 4 AND, OR and NOT gates [L-meta-19122]: when one wire a side is on, one NOT stands in for the OR of all the others. The saving grows only linearly, nothing above that, so it is not a wall.",
